1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:05,250
Lesson 12, Bob's big cookie order.

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:08,710
The family is gathered around the dinner table.

3
00:00:09,339 --> 00:00:11,849
Bob tells them about his deal with the village market.

4
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:14,990
He asks his kids for help baking the cookies.

5
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:20,689
I know I've been down to the dumps since I got fired, but things are looking up now.

6
00:00:21,019 --> 00:00:22,910
The village market wants to sell our cookies.

7
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:25,070
That's great news, Dad.

8
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:27,889
But we're going to have to bake like crazy over the weekend.

9
00:00:27,739 --> 00:00:30,029
They want 2,000 cookies by Monday.

10
00:00:30,519 --> 00:00:32,609
2,000 cookies in three days?

11
00:00:32,979 --> 00:00:35,309
Don't you think you've bitten off more than you can chew?

12
00:00:35,619 --> 00:00:39,070
Yeah, you're going to be running around like a chicken with its head cut off.

13
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:41,309
Fortunately, there are four of us here.

14
00:00:41,539 --> 00:00:43,250
You kids will have to pitch in too.

15
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:45,929
Sorry, but I can't.

16
00:00:46,119 --> 00:00:48,149
I have to finish Ted's chemistry homework.

17
00:00:48,399 --> 00:00:50,670
Then I've got to get going on my election speech.

18
00:00:51,079 --> 00:00:53,329
What's that about doing Ted's chemistry homework?

19
00:00:53,579 --> 00:00:54,409
Never mind.

20
00:00:54,659 --> 00:00:56,890
Amber will help out with the cookies instead of Nicole.

21
00:00:56,740 --> 00:01:01,729
For heaven's sake, Nicole, it's like pulling teeth getting you to do any work around here.

